<title>AUSTRALIA: Sydney hotel bed tax to be phased in - NSW govt.</title>
<headline>Sydney hotel bed tax to be phased in - NSW govt.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-07-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>The New South Wales government said on Tuesday it would phase in its central Sydney hotel bed tax at a reduced rate over a 12-month period in a compromise move to resolve a dispute with the hotel industry.</p>
<p>The government said the tax would be reduced from 10 percent to five percent at the start of the phasing-in period in September, but only for hotels that enter agreements to provide rooms for the Sydney 2000 Olympic Games organising body, SOCOG.</p>
</text>
